    "result_text": "The build passes with all tests green. Here's a summary of what I implemented.\n\n## Change: level rules \u2192 points system\n\n**New scoring model** (in a single dedicated helper, `MembershipPoints`): score starts at 0 and adds +2 for an email, +1 when `namesakeCount == 0`, +2 for a household of 3+, +3 for tenure over 365 days; the score maps to a level (1 for 0\u20131, 2 for 2\u20133, 3 for 4\u20135, 4 for 6+). Both `membershipPoints` and `membershipLevel` are now returned.\n\n### Files changed\n\n- **`MembershipPoints.java`** (new) \u2014 owns the points formula and the points\u2192level mapping as small pure functions. All the rule constants live here, isolating the \"points system\" as one cohesive unit.\n- **`Household.java`** \u2014 added a `size(householdId, owners)` counter, keeping household-membership logic with the household concept (reused by the step rather than duplicated).\n- **`AssignMembershipLevel.java`** \u2014 rewritten to just orchestrate: gather the four factors (email, namesake count, household size, tenure days), delegate scoring/mapping to `MembershipPoints`, and store both fields. It now takes `OwnerRepository` to size the household (the new owner isn't persisted yet, so it's counted with a `+1`).\n- **`Owner.java`** \u2014 added the `membershipPoints` field with `@Column(name = \"membership_points\")` and accessors.\n- **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added the read-only `membershipPoints` property (so the generated `OwnerDto` carries it and MapStruct maps it by name) and updated the `membershipLevel` description/`maximum` to reflect the new 1\u20134 range.\n- **DB schemas** (hsqldb, h2, mysql, postgres) \u2014 added the `membership_points INTEGER` column.\n- **`AuditOwnerCreated.java`** \u2014 the audit line now logs `membershipPoints` alongside `membershipLevel`.\n\n### Verification\n\n`mvn test` \u2192 **BUILD SUCCESS**, `Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0`. The acceptance test's fresh owner (email + no namesake, single-member household, zero tenure) scores 3 points \u2192 level 2, matching the audit line `membershipPoints=3 membershipLevel=2`.",
